From 1a06f8166abffda349cd2b0f3a3c12b0a202eaf6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arnaud Le Blanc <arnaud.lb@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:02:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 09/12] Fix GHSA-658j-r8rw-q6mx:
 session.upload_progress.enabled is off by default

Also prevent changes to session INI settings at runtime when
session.upload_progress.enabled is On.

(cherry picked from commit 3f70f66611583bca4ec18385f7f407e2808fa61f)

PHP 8.1 adaptation:
- 8.1 checks SESSION_CHECK_OUTPUT_STATE before SESSION_CHECK_ACTIVE_STATE in
  OnUpdateSessionBool, OnUpdateSidLength and OnUpdateSidBits; the new guard
  is added first and the 8.1 order is kept.
- 8.1 still has the separate OnUpdateTransSid (session.use_trans_sid) and
  OnUpdateLazyWrite (session.lazy_write) handlers, which 8.2 folded into
  OnUpdateSessionBool; both get the guard too, matching 8.2 coverage.
- 8.1 registers session.cookie_samesite with plain OnUpdateString (8.2 uses
  the guarded OnUpdateSessionString); a new OnUpdateSessionSameSite applies
  only the upload-progress guard, so 8.1 does not gain the active/output
  state checks it never had.
- PHP_GINIT: 8.1 has no in_rfc1867_update global; only rfc1867_enabled is
  initialised.
Note: the 8.1 "Avoid state corruption via bailout" mitigation already makes
php_session_rfc1867_callback() a no-op, so this is defence in depth here.
---
 ext/session/session.c                         |  30 ++++-
 ...ssion_ini_set_upload_progress_enabled.phpt | 127 ++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 155 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 ext/session/tests/session_ini_set_upload_progress_enabled.phpt

